# Inspection — Thuế tài sản ở Việt Nam: ưu và nhược

Inspector: independent (did not receive a maker's summary)
Axis: whole (`normal` lane — result · steps · plan · honesty)
Artifact read: `03-deliverable.md` (direct, in full, before opening `03-receipts.md`)
Inspected-sha: 7823c7bbf8bc0deb78a477d59377dbb682cd79e25dfc29a59516d1ca4de1543d

Verify scope: **Egress blocked session-wide** — probed once, directly, by attempting
`WebFetch https://vneconomy.vn/` (a domain the deliverable cites twice). Returned
`{"error_type":"EGRESS_BLOCKED","domain":"vneconomy.vn","message":"Access to vneconomy.vn
is blocked by the network egress proxy."}`. No further fetches attempted.
**Sources opened: 0 of the 15 cited. Sources sampled: 0. Liveness of cited links:
unverifiable. Nothing is promoted to grade A; B is the honest ceiling for this inspection
exactly as it was for the run.** `Bash` and `Edit` are also disabled in this session, so
the sha above is the one supplied by the orchestrator (not independently recomputed) and
the word count below is manual, not scripted — stated so it can be discounted accordingly.

Verification therefore consisted of (a) tracing every figure, rate, threshold, date, name
and attribution in the deliverable back to `01-research.md` (value, year, base, source
domain), (b) internal-consistency checks including the prose↔confidence-table match in
both directions, (c) arithmetic sanity on the one ratio the piece carries, (d) plan
compliance against `00-brief.md` (five movements, 700–950 word band, locked lexicon), and
(e) an audit of `03-receipts.md` against the page, performed last.

Threshold used, stated up front: **FIX-IT** = checkably false, unsupported, or
self-contradictory *as shipped* against the run's own fact store. **Minor** = anything I
would merely have written differently. Minors do not enter the verdict.

## Findings

### [result] One FIX-IT: an unsourced proposition asserted as fact, propped up by a figure for a different quantity

Deliverable, "Phía ủng hộ":

> "**Bất động sản chiếm phần lớn tài sản hộ gia đình Việt Nam** — tỷ lệ hộ sở hữu nhà
> ~90%, cao hơn Mỹ, Úc, Indonesia [B, thitruongtaichinhtiente.vn] — nên đánh thuế tài
> sản là đánh đúng nơi của cải tập trung."

`01-research.md` records the opposite of support for the main clause, twice and
explicitly:

- Key findings: "đây là tỷ lệ **hộ có nhà**, không phải tỷ trọng bất động sản trong tổng
  tài sản hộ gia đình (**không tìm được số trực tiếp cho chỉ tiêu này**)".
- Open conflicts / gaps: "Không tìm được số liệu chính thức, có nguồn, cho 'tỷ trọng bất
  động sản trong tổng tài sản hộ gia đình Việt Nam' … chỉ có tỷ lệ hộ sở hữu nhà (90%) và
  tỷ trọng BĐS trong tài sản thế chấp ngân hàng (73%) — **hai đại lượng khác, không nên
  thay thế cho nhau**."

Three separable defects in one sentence:

1. The main clause is a claim the fact store records as **not found**. It ships ungraded
   and uncited.
2. The 90% home-ownership rate is placed, in an em-dash appositive carrying a
   `[B, source]` tag, as the evidence *for* that clause — the exact substitution research
   forbade. A source is credited, inside this sentence, with carrying a proposition it does
   not carry. (The 90% figure and the "cao hơn Mỹ, Úc, Indonesia" comparison are themselves
   accurate to research: 66% / 66% / 84% are all below 90%. The error is what the figure is
   made to prove, not the figure.)
3. It is load-bearing, not decorative: the conclusion drawn from it — "đánh thuế tài sản
   là đánh đúng nơi của cải tập trung" — is one of the three pillars of the pro-side
   movement. Remove the premise and the pillar goes with it.

This also breaks the confidence table in the prose→table direction: table row 8 covers only
"Tỷ lệ hộ sở hữu nhà VN ~90%, cao hơn Mỹ/Úc/Indonesia". The stronger claim actually
asserted in the body has no row, no grade and no source anywhere in the artifact.

**Independently corroborated by the maker's own receipts** (audited after this finding was
written — see the receipts section): `03-receipts.md` lists this very point under
"Đã KHÔNG đưa vào bài" and states "bài **chỉ** dùng tỷ lệ hộ sở hữu nhà (90%)". The page
does not match that account: the sentence's main clause asserts the household-asset share
outright. So the rule was known and the exclusion was intended — the sentence simply
escaped it. That makes the repair small and low-risk, and it also means the receipts
overstate what the page does.

Note in the maker's favour, and it does not rescue the sentence: `00-brief.md`'s outline
for movement 3 did ask for "tỷ trọng tài sản hộ gia đình nằm trong bất động sản". Research
then found no such figure. That is precisely the situation Axiom 7 covers — say out loud
that the new information broke the plan and write the point as a limitation, or drop it.
Writing it as established fact is the defect.

**Required fix:** either (a) drop the main clause and let the 90% ownership rate carry only
what research supports (widespread home ownership → a broad base, wide incidence), or
(b) keep the point but write it as what it is — no sourced Vietnamese figure exists for
real estate's share of household assets; the available proxies (90% ownership, 73% of bank
collateral) measure different things and are not substitutes. Whichever is chosen, the
confidence table must gain a matching row, and `03-receipts.md` must be brought back into
line with the page.

### [result] Everything else traced clean

The rest of the artifact holds up against the fact store, item by item:

- **0,03–0,15%**, land only, no tax on housing, Luật 2010 — matches research.
- **~1.700 tỷ đồng/năm, ~0,14% tổng thu NSNN**, attributed to Bộ Tài chính via
  vneconomy.vn — matches research verbatim. Arithmetic sanity: 1.700 ÷ 0,0014 ≈ 1,21
  triệu tỷ đồng of implied total revenue, an order-of-magnitude-plausible state budget, so
  the two numbers are at least mutually consistent. No arithmetic was introduced by the
  maker; none is wrong.
- **Three instruments stay distinct.** The section is built around the distinction
  ("Ba thứ hay bị gộp làm một"). *Tiền sử dụng đất* is described as a one-off levy on State
  allocation, "gần với phí giao dịch hơn là thuế", explicitly "hai khoản khác bản chất,
  không nên gộp thành 'thuế tài sản'". No conflation anywhere in the piece; the trap
  research warned about ("thuế tài sản chiếm X% ngân sách") is not committed.
- **Three proposals, three dates, none merged, none written as law.** The 2018 draft (>700
  triệu, 0,4%/năm) is tied to the shelved bill and to public opposition; the PIT
  holding-period amendment carries "**dự kiến trình** Quốc hội khoảng tháng 10/2026" — a
  submission date, correctly not a passage date; the second-home / vacant-property idea is
  "mới ở mức nghiên cứu". Closing line: "Ba đề xuất, ba thời điểm — không cái nào là luật."
  No proposed rate is written as enacted.
- **The disputed land-revenue share reads as unsettled.** All three figures are given with
  their bases and periods (6,6% tổng thu, không rõ năm / 14,7% ngân sách địa phương
  2012–2017 / 15–16% gần đây) and the piece states "ba số không cùng kỳ, không chọn một số
  duy nhất", concluding only what is safe to conclude. Correct handling.
- **No Vietnam-versus-OECD property-tax ratio is constructed.** The forbidden inputs —
  OECD's ~1% of GDP, the 5,1% of total tax take, Vietnam's 16,8% tax-to-GDP (2023), the
  19,5% / 33,9% comparators — appear nowhere in the deliverable. The only cross-country
  rate comparison (0,03% vs 1–1,5%) sits *inside a named expert's argument* and is held in
  research as that expert's own statement. The piece does not build the aggregate
  comparison in its own voice. Clean.
- **Đặng Hùng Võ** is rendered accurately on both sides: rate too low / supports taxing
  second homes / tax cannot fix supply-demand price rises, only the speculative "giá ảo"
  (research's own quoted term, correctly kept in quotes); and, in the opposition section,
  the income-level warning against Singapore-style rates, correctly characterised as an
  argument about *timing*, not principle. Research's phrase "không bền vững" is paraphrased
  rather than dressed up as a quote — the right call.
- **HoREA** and **Bộ Tài chính** items match research's content and attributions.

### [result] The opposition case — checked hardest, and it holds

Seven of research's eight opposition arguments are present, and the seven are exactly the
seven the brief's movement-4 outline specified. The omitted one (#5, subdued market /
liquidity) was not in the plan, and its removal is disclosed with a reason in
`03-receipts.md` — plan-compliant, not scope drift.

None of the seven is softened. "Người mua ở thực gánh chi phí chứ không phải nhà đầu cơ" is
stated flatly, in bold; the urban–rural inequity keeps its concrete bite (two small
provincial plots taxed harder than one central villa); the fact that a *supporter* of the
tax is also one of its most credible brakes is used rather than buried.

The two arguments research recorded as unattributed are the specific thing to check, and
the artifact gets both directions right:

- **Present.** Asset-rich / cash-poor ("hộ 'giàu tài sản, nghèo tiền mặt'") and evasion via
  nominee ownership or plot-splitting are both in the body, at full argumentative strength,
  each with its mechanism spelled out.
- **Marked, not dressed up.** The paragraph opens "Hai lập luận sau **không truy được tên**
  trong lần tìm kiếm này, nhưng vẫn phải nêu chứ không bỏ vì thiếu tên", and both table
  rows read "B (không truy được tác giả cụ thể tại Việt Nam) — không có nguồn quy kết —
  nêu như lập luận, không như phát biểu có tên". Neither is given a borrowed citation.
- The closing sentence — "không vì thiếu tên mà kém sức nặng hơn các lập luận có tên ở
  trên" — states the principle rather than letting the reader discount them silently.

This is the part of the brief most at risk, and it was executed correctly.

### [sources] Verification, and the ceiling

Egress probe: attempted once, refused (`vneconomy.vn`, EGRESS_BLOCKED — full response in
the Verify-scope line above). The run's own preflight records `Egress: BLOCKED
(2026-09-02T16:07:02Z)` and research records a matching failed WebFetch on
thuvienphapluat.vn, so the block is consistent across all three stations. **Zero sources
opened, zero sampled.** I could not confirm that a single cited domain is live, could not
check any snippet against its page, and did not attempt to reason my way to a grade-A
substitute.

What that means for the verdict: I can certify that every number, date, rate, threshold,
name and attribution in the deliverable **traces to `01-research.md` with the same value,
same year, same base and same source domain** — with the one exception above. I cannot
certify that `01-research.md` is right about the world. The artifact says exactly this in
its own first body line — "Egress bị chặn khi làm bài này … không claim nào được gắn A —
tất cả dừng ở B" — in plain body prose, not only in the table, which is what was required.

### [steps] Claimed steps vs. what is visible on the page

Reached before opening `03-receipts.md`. The discipline the brief demands is not merely
asserted in the artifact, it is *visible* in it: the disputed-figure handling, the
three-way instrument split, the "dự kiến trình" hedge, the unattributed-argument
labelling, and a confidence table in which all 15 rows are B and 2 carry an explicit
attribution-failure note. No step is claimed on the page that the page does not show. The
one place where the receipts claim more restraint than the page delivers is recorded in the
FIX-IT above and in the receipts audit below.

### [plan] Followed, with the deviations already published

- **Five movements + table**: all present, in order (mở → ba thứ hay bị gộp → phía ủng hộ →
  phía phản đối → kết → bảng độ tin cậy).
- **700–950 word band**: my manual count of the body (headings and title included, table
  excluded) lands at roughly 870–890 space-delimited tokens; the maker's receipts report
  910 by `\S+` match. The two counts differ by under 5%, which is inside manual-counting
  error, and **both sit inside the band**, so the band holds on either figure. `Bash` is
  disabled, so neither I nor a script could settle it more precisely here. Per-movement
  lengths sit close to the outline's targets (opening ~95 incl. the egress line vs ~80;
  distinction ~143 vs ~140; pro ~190 vs ~230; con ~314 vs ~280; close ~98 vs ~120). The
  split running slightly toward the opposition is consistent with the brief's instruction
  that the opposition be given at full strength.
- **Locked lexicon**: "thuế sử dụng đất phi nông nghiệp" / "tiền sử dụng đất" / "thuế tài
  sản" are kept apart throughout; "dự thảo/đề xuất" is never written as "luật"; projected
  dates carry "dự kiến". One partial miss on the house rule "mọi số kèm nguồn + năm" — see
  minors.
- **Announced deviations** in `00-brief.md` (Gate 1 skipped; research +46%; plan +67%) are
  published under a "Sai lệch có công bố (R4)" heading, which is the correct handling of
  Axiom 8. Not counted against the artifact.

### [honesty] Grading is correct; one claim is pitched above its evidence

- **No grade A anywhere.** All 15 table rows are B, and the ceiling is disclosed in body
  prose. Correct for a blocked-egress run.
- **No D leaked in.** No guess is presented as fact; the one place research had nothing
  (the two unattributed arguments) is labelled rather than filled in.
- **Confidence table ↔ prose, table→prose direction: clean.** All 15 rows correspond to
  claims actually made in the body; no row describes something the piece does not say.
- **prose→table direction: one gap**, the FIX-IT above. A second, smaller ungraded
  assertion is noted in minors.
- The two-way honesty test on the unattributed arguments — included *and* not
  source-dressed — passes.

## Minors (not blocking)

These are things I would have written differently, or small imprecisions that do not make
any sentence false. **None of them enters the verdict**, and none should be treated as a
FIX-IT in a later round.

1. **"chưa có dự thảo"** (proposal 3) drops research's qualifier "chính thức trình Quốc
   hội". Research's own recommended phrasing was "chưa có dự thảo luật chính thức". The
   shorter form asserts marginally more absence than the fact store holds.
2. **Missing years on two figures.** House style says "mọi số kèm nguồn + năm". The
   ~1.700 tỷ đồng / 0,14% pair and the ~90% ownership rate carry no year — because research
   holds none. The piece already models the honest fix elsewhere ("6,6% … (không rõ năm)")
   and could apply it here.
3. **"vốn cạn dần khi quỹ đất công hết"** (pro section) is an ungraded, uncited assertion
   with no table row. Read as a conditional it is close to tautological, which is why it is
   not a FIX-IT, but it is the one sentence in the piece carrying no provenance at all.
4. **"15–16% gần đây"** loses the base ("thu ngân sách địa phương") that research attaches
   to it. Parallelism with the preceding clause probably carries it for most readers, but
   spelling it out costs three words and the entire point of that sentence is that the
   bases differ.
5. **Bare `[B]`** on the cost-pass-through claim, where every neighbouring claim carries
   `[B, source]`. Sources do exist in table row 12 (wiki.batdongsan.com.vn,
   thoibaonganhang.vn). As printed, a reader may mistake it for a third unattributed
   argument, which undersells it.
6. **HoREA is never expanded** (Hiệp hội Bất động sản TP.HCM) for a general-audience piece,
   and the ministry assigned to build the parcel-level land-price database (Bộ Nông nghiệp
   & Môi trường) is unnamed. Both are in research.
7. **Rate basis unstated** in the Võ comparison: 0,03% is levied on an area-based
   assessment, foreign rates of 1–1,5% on value. Research flags the asymmetry; the piece
   passes the comparison through as the expert's own words, which is defensible, but one
   clause would close it.
8. **Tiền sử dụng đất** is defined only as arising "khi Nhà nước giao đất"; research also
   includes permission to change land-use purpose.

## Receipts audit

Performed **after** the findings above were written, and treated as a claim to audit, not a
briefing. Checked each receipts assertion against the page:

| Receipts claim | Visible on the page? |
|---|---|
| Built only from `01-research.md`, ceiling B inherited, nothing raised to A | Yes — all 15 rows B, disclosure in body prose |
| Five movements per the outline + table | Yes |
| Three instruments not conflated; projected date not written as passed | Yes |
| Three land-share figures given as not-same-period, no single number chosen | Yes |
| 5 named + 2 unattributed opposition arguments, the latter kept and labelled | Yes |
| Conclusion states conditions, does not rule "nên/không nên" | Yes |
| No VN-vs-OECD numeric comparison constructed | Yes — none of the forbidden aggregates appears |
| Argument #5 (subdued market) cut, with reason | Yes — absence confirmed, reason disclosed |
| **"bài chỉ dùng tỷ lệ hộ sở hữu nhà (90%)"**, household-asset share excluded | **No — the body asserts the household-asset share outright.** See FIX-IT |
| Body measured at 910 words by `\S+` | Not reproducible here (`Bash` disabled); my manual count ~870–890, same side of the band |

One discrepancy, and it is the same defect the artifact-first read had already surfaced —
which is the point of doing the audit second. The receipts describe an exclusion the page
did not carry out. Everything else the receipts assert about the work is visible in the
work.

## Verdict: FIX-IT

One blocking defect, in the pro-side movement of `03-deliverable.md` ("Phía ủng hộ"):

**Required fix (single item):** the sentence "Bất động sản chiếm phần lớn tài sản hộ gia
đình Việt Nam — tỷ lệ hộ sở hữu nhà ~90% … — nên đánh thuế tài sản là đánh đúng nơi của
cải tập trung" asserts as fact a proposition `01-research.md` records as **not found**
("không tìm được số trực tiếp cho chỉ tiêu này"), and uses the 90% home-ownership rate as
its evidence — the substitution research explicitly forbids ("hai đại lượng khác, không nên
thay thế cho nhau"). It ships ungraded, uncited and absent from the confidence table, while
a `[B, thitruongtaichinhtiente.vn]` tag inside the same sentence lends it borrowed
authority; `03-receipts.md` meanwhile claims the piece excluded exactly this. Either drop
the main clause and keep only what the 90% figure supports, or retain the point and mark it
as an evidence gap (no sourced Vietnamese figure for real estate's share of household
assets; 90% ownership and 73% of bank collateral measure different things). Add or correct
the matching confidence-table row, and align `03-receipts.md` with whatever the page then
says.

Everything else in the artifact — the three-instrument distinction, the three proposals and
their three dates, the unresolved land-revenue share, the absence of any Vietnam-vs-OECD
ratio, the opposition case including both unattributed arguments correctly present *and*
correctly marked, the all-B grading with the ceiling disclosed in body prose, the five
movements and the word band — passes. The minors listed above are explicitly **not** grounds
for a further FIX-IT round: if a later round finds only items of that kind, the verdict is
PASS.
